## Usage

{% if needs_service_stack %}
The backing service{% if database == 'postgres' and include_celery %}s{% endif %}
({% if database == 'postgres' %}Postgres{% endif %}{% if database == 'postgres' and include_celery %} and {% endif %}{% if include_celery %}Redis{% endif %})
live in `docker-compose.yml`. It is **not** part of the devcontainer — bring it up from
inside the container with the in-container Docker daemon:

```console
$ docker compose up -d
$ cp .env.example .env
$ uv run python manage.py migrate
$ uv run python manage.py runserver
```
{% else %}
```console
$ cp .env.example .env
$ uv run python manage.py migrate
$ uv run python manage.py runserver
```
{% endif %}

The API is served under `/api/`, with a health check at `/api/health/`{% if api_docs == 'drf-spectacular' %} and an OpenAPI schema at `/api/schema/`{% endif %}.

## Development

```console
$ uv run pytest          # run the test suite
$ uv run ruff check .     # lint
$ uv run ruff format .    # format
```
